@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    var retentionDays = ViewData["EventSubPayloadRetentionDays"] as int? ?? 14;
    var supportContactEmail = ViewData["SupportContactEmail"] as string;
}

<h1 class="mb-1">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<p class="text-muted">Last updated: @DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("MMMM d, yyyy")</p>

<div class="alert alert-secondary">
    This policy explains what information Twitch Tools ("we", "us", "the Service") collects when you connect your
    Twitch, Discord, or Bluesky accounts, why we collect it, and how it is stored and protected. It applies to
    streamers who sign in to the Service ("you", "streamer") as well as to viewers whose public chat activity is
    observed while using the Service's viewer tracking features.
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">1. Who We Are</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            Twitch Tools is a self-hosted suite of tools for streamers, including overlays, timed chat
            messages, EventSub-driven notifications, viewer watch-time statistics, and optional Discord and Bluesky
            integrations.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">2. Information We Collect</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5>Account &amp;amp; Sign-in Data</h5>
        <p>
            When you sign in via our identity provider (Keycloak), we receive and store your unique subject
            identifier and, where provided, your email address, so we can associate your streamer profile and
            settings with your account.
        </p>

        <h5>Twitch Connection Data</h5>
        <p>
            When you connect your Twitch account (and optionally a separate bot account), we store your Twitch user
            ID, client ID, and OAuth access/refresh tokens. These tokens are <strong>encrypted at rest</strong> and
            are used only to call the Twitch API on your behalf &mdash; for example, to read chat, send messages,
            check stream status, and register EventSub subscriptions.
        </p>

        <h5>Viewer Statistics</h5>
        <p>
            While you are live, the Service periodically records which Twitch accounts are present in your chat and
            accumulates their total watch time. We store the viewer's Twitch user ID and total seconds watched per
            stream session &mdash; we do <em>not</em> store viewers' chat message content. Viewer display names are
            resolved on demand from the Twitch API and are not persisted. Streamers can identify and exclude known
            bot accounts (e.g. chat bots such as Nightbot or StreamElements) from these statistics; a list of known
            bot accounts is maintained centrally by the Service administrator and is not personal data about any
            individual streamer or viewer.
        </p>

        <h5>Chat, Follower &amp;amp; Subscriber Events</h5>
        <p>
            We store records of live/offline transitions, new followers, and new subscribers (Twitch user ID,
            login, and display name where available) so we can drive overlays and social-media announcements, and we
            keep a log of timed chat messages you configure.
        </p>

        <h5>EventSub Diagnostic Payloads</h5>
        <p>
            If enabled, raw Twitch EventSub webhook payloads may be logged for troubleshooting purposes. When
            enabled, these are retained for @retentionDays day@(retentionDays == 1 ? "" : "s") before being purged,
            based on the Service's configured retention setting. However, this is only enabled when required.
        </p>

        <h5>Discord Integration</h5>
        <p>
            If you connect Discord, we store the Discord guild (server) ID and schedule-sync configuration needed to
            keep your Discord server's events in sync with your Twitch schedule.
        </p>

        <h5>Bluesky Integration</h5>
        <p>
            If you connect Bluesky, we store your Bluesky identifier and app password (encrypted at rest) solely to
            post "going live" / "stream ended" announcements on your behalf, along with the post templates you
            configure.
        </p>

        <h5>Custom Overlays</h5>
        <p>
            Any custom overlay HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and field data you create is stored so it can be rendered by
            your browser source in your streaming software.
        </p>

        <h5>Technical Data</h5>
        <p class="mb-0">
            Like most web applications, our hosting and error-monitoring infrastructure may automatically log
            request metadata (such as IP address, timestamps, and error details) for security and diagnostic
            purposes.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">3. How We Use Information</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li>To authenticate you and operate your streamer dashboard.</li>
            <li>To call the Twitch, Discord, and Bluesky APIs on your behalf for the features you enable.</li>
            <li>To display viewer watch-time statistics and overlays to you.</li>
            <li>To diagnose and fix problems with EventSub notifications and other integrations.</li>
            <li>To maintain the security and integrity of the Service.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">4. Legal Basis &amp;amp; Viewer Data</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            Streamer account data is processed on the basis of your consent when you connect an account and your
            ongoing use of the Service. Viewer watch-time data is derived from publicly visible Twitch chat presence
            and is processed on the basis of the streamer's legitimate interest in understanding their own audience.
            Viewers do not create accounts with the Service and cannot be contacted by us directly; requests to
            access or remove viewer watch-time data should be directed to the relevant streamer, who can delete this
            data from their dashboard or by contacting the Service administrator.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">5. Sharing of Information</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p>We do not sell your data. We share information only:</p>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li>With Twitch, Discord, and Bluesky, as required to operate the integrations you enable.</li>
            <li>Where required by law or to protect the rights, property, or safety of the Service, its users, or others.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">6. Data Retention</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            We retain streamer profile, connection, and statistics data for as long as your account remains
            connected to the Service, plus a reasonable period thereafter for backups and legal compliance.
            EventSub diagnostic payloads (if logging is enabled) are retained for @retentionDays day@(retentionDays == 1 ? "" : "s")
            and then automatically deleted. You may disconnect integrations or request deletion of your account and
            associated data at any time.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">7. Security</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            Sensitive credentials &mdash; including Twitch OAuth tokens and Bluesky app passwords &mdash; are
            encrypted at rest. Access to the administration area is restricted to authorised administrators. No
            method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">8. Your Rights &amp; Choices</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, export, or delete your personal
            data, and to withdraw consent by disconnecting a service. You can manage most of your connections and
            data directly from the Tools section of the dashboard, or contact us using the details in Section 1 to
            make a request.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">9. Children's Privacy</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            The Service is intended for use by Twitch streamers and is not directed at children. We do not
            knowingly collect personal data from children under the age required by Twitch's own terms of service.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">10. Changes to This Policy</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by updating the "Last
            updated" date at the top of this page.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header">11. Contact Us</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-0">
            If you have questions about this policy or wish to exercise your data rights, please contact
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(supportContactEmail))
            {
                <a href="mailto:@supportContactEmail">@supportContactEmail</a>
            }
            else
            {
                <code>[operator contact email]</code>
            }
            .
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
